# Local checkouts and scan outputs — never shared, regenerated by `make clone`/analysis.
work/
reports/
!reports/.gitkeep

# Real target data. NEVER commit a production dump here — the lab's own finding L1 was
# exactly this kind of dump becoming reachable from the LAN (20,368 real people). Seed with
# synthetic data instead. This ignore is a backstop for this one known file, not a blanket
# rule — other db-init/*.sql files (seeds, notes) are meant to be versioned.
targets/costos_web/db-init/01_data.sql

# Dedicated deploy key for `make clone` (never the operator's own ~/.ssh — see recipe L2).
configs/deploy_key*

.env.local
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc
node_modules/
.venv/

# Profiles whose accounts are REAL, not lab-synthetic. targets/*/target.env is meant to be
# versioned — it is the contract between the lab and a project — but that only holds while the
# credentials in it are throwaway. `movil` carries actual Zajuna logins (national ID numbers and
# personal passwords) because that stack has no synthetic accounts to test authorization with.
# Publishing them is irreversible: a push to a hosted remote writes them into history for good.
# Rule: a profile whose ROLE_A_/ROLE_B_ are real accounts stays out of the repository.
targets/movil/

# La otra mitad de esa misma regla. Un perfil no nace con cuentas reales: `costos_web` empezó
# con localhost y cuentas sembradas, y se volvió peligroso el día que se le apuntó al despliegue
# de validación. Excluir el perfil entero, como `movil`, cuesta el contrato versionado; el
# override local lo conserva. target.env se versiona y declara QUÉ variables existen;
# target.env.local trae los valores reales y no sale de esta máquina. La plantilla
# target.env.local.example sí se versiona: es la que dice qué rellenar.
targets/*/target.env.local

# Editor settings — not part of the lab.
.vscode/

# Platform baselines: snapshots of a real Moodle (110 MB dump + 66 MB code tree). Regenerated
# from the source server with tools/moodle-snapshot.sh, and too large for git — but the MANIFEST
# is versioned, so which baseline a run used stays reviewable.
baselines/*/*.dump
baselines/*/*.tar.zst
